      "titre": "Intuition : ce que j'aime",
      "niveau": "pour démarrer",
      "paragraphes": [
        "**I like pizza.** (J'aime la pizza.) **I don't like fish.** (Je n'aime pas le poisson.) **Do you like apples ?** — **Yes, I do.** / **No, I don't.** Aliments : bread, milk, cheese, apple, banana, chicken, rice, water."
      ],
      "exemple": {
        "titre": "Exemple",
        "etapes": [
          "I like cheese.",
          "I don't like milk.",
          "Do you like bananas ? — Yes, I do."
        ]
      },
      "aRetenir": "Négation : don't + verbe."
    },
    {
      "titre": "Le présent simple",
      "niveau": "CM2",
      "paragraphes": [
        "Pour parler des habitudes : **I get up at seven.** **I go to school.** **I play football.** À la 3e personne du singulier, on ajoute -s : **He plays football.** **She likes music.** La question : **Do you play ?** / **Does he play ?**"
      ],
      "exemple": {
        "titre": "Exemple : ma journée",
        "etapes": [
          "I get up at 7.",
          "I eat breakfast.",
          "I go to school at 8."
        ]
      },
      "aRetenir": "He / she / it : verbe + s."
    }
  ],
